Lukearch live environment marker
================================

This live root filesystem is generated from the lukearch archiso profile.

Important:
- Lukearch is Arch-based and unofficial.
- The live image starts the KDE Plasma desktop through SDDM.
- The desktop session uses a locked local account with sudo available to the
  `wheel` group after the user sets a password.
- Run `sudo passwd lukearch` once to set the desktop account password. This
  password is for logging in again; it does not authorize sudo.
- Run `sudo lukearch-set-admin-password` once to set the separate administrator
  password. It asks for the desktop account password first, then sets the root
  password. After that, sudo asks for the administrator password, and the
  command refuses to run again.
- Keyboard and mouse input use generic libinput drivers. No GPU-specific
  driver is forced into the image; install the driver matching the hardware
  with pacman when a persistent system is available.
- Inbound network traffic is blocked by default; SSH is not installed.
- This is an ephemeral live image. Do not store sensitive data in the live
  session, and install security updates promptly on a persistent system.
- ARM/Apple silicon support is tracked in docs/arm-support.md in the repository.
